  "label": "antisemitic stereotype mapped onto visual scene",
  "description": "The text 'only israelis can knocks the teeth out of a 6 yr old girl' is mapped onto the visual of the young girl covered in blood and holding an apple. This mapping uses the visual of the child (a symbol of innocence) to represent the victim in the antisemitic blood libel trope, while the text explicitly assigns the violent act to 'Israelis'. The visual material (the child with blood and apple) is used to instantiate the hateful stereotype described in the text.",
